#!/usr/bin/env bash
#
# mirror-streak - Agora - the GitHub mirror's conclusion is PUSHED, not pulled (T-0623).
#
# THE DEFECT, WHICH IS A MEASUREMENT AND NOT A WORRY.
#
# On 2026-09-19 the mirror's only workflow was found to have failed on NINE consecutive runs
# since 2026-08-27. Three weeks. An email to the maintainer on every push, and nobody looked.
# D-020 keeps that workflow as an informative second opinion and says, in its own words, that it
# "may fail without blocking, but it may never lie" - and the half about lying had quietly
# stopped holding.
#
# tests/bin/watch-gate was given a mirror section the same day, and it is good: it reads the
# runs, counts the streak, names the conclusions and refuses to let an absence read as good news.
# But it only runs WHEN SOMEBODY TYPES THE COMMAND, which is the same detection property as the
# email that had just been missed nine times. A conclusion nobody is obliged to read is a
# conclusion nobody reads.
#
# This script is what looks, on every push, from inside the pipeline.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE OBJECTION THIS FILE HAD TO ANSWER FIRST, AND HALF OF IT WAS FALSE.
#
# watch-gate's own comment says an invariant here "would need the network and a GitHub token
# inside `agora-invariants`, a job that runs in a drupalci container which has neither", and
# concludes that "a gate that goes red because a token is absent is a gate somebody makes
# permissive within the week".
#
# The conclusion is right and the premise about the TOKEN is not. Measured 2026-09-21, before
# this file was written, with no credentials of any kind:
#
#   GET https://api.github.com/repos/<slug>                          -> 200
#   GET https://api.github.com/repos/<slug>/actions/workflows        -> 200
#   GET https://api.github.com/repos/<slug>/actions/runs?branch=1.x  -> 200, total_count 157
#
# The mirror is a PUBLIC repository and GitHub's Actions API answers anonymously for one.
# X-RateLimit-Limit comes back as 60 an hour for an unauthenticated caller, and this script makes
# three requests. NO TOKEN IS USED OR NEEDED, and that is the whole reason this can exist at all.
#
# The network half of the objection stands, and is answered the way tests/bin/ported-drift and
# the theme's tests/bin/upstream-drift answer it: a runner that cannot reach the API is a THIRD
# STATE that exits 2, prints the sentence that negates the misreading, and is tolerated by the
# gate. It is never a pass.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BLOCKING ON PROVENANCE, REPORTING ON THE STREAK. The shape is tests/bin/ported-drift's, and it
# is deliberate in both directions.
#
# PROVENANCE BLOCKS, and every one of these is fixable by a commit in THIS repository:
#
#   * a workflow file exists under .github/workflows/ that is not declared below
#   * a workflow is declared below that has no file under .github/workflows/
#   * the API's `full_name` for the declared slug is not the declared slug
#   * the mirror has RUN a workflow whose path is not declared below
#   * a local `github` remote exists and does not parse to the declared slug
#
# The fourth is the one that matters most and it is the reason the list is declared rather than
# discovered. D-009(d) and T-804 put visual regression on this mirror. A second workflow whose
# conclusion nobody reads would reproduce the original defect exactly, one file over.
#
# THE STREAK REPORTS. A red mirror does NOT turn this pipeline red. D-020 makes drupalcode the
# gate and the mirror informative, and promoting a red mirror to a failed gate here would be a
# signed decision taken by a tool instead of by a person. It would also be the exact shape
# D-023(5) exists to refuse: a gate that fails for a reason no commit here can address is a gate
# somebody makes permissive, arriving through the door marked "more rigour".
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BUT A STREAK MUST NOT BE ABLE TO STAND FOR THREE WEEKS AGAIN, WHICH IS THE WHOLE COMPLAINT.
# So there is a cap on the AGE of the streak, and past it the streak becomes a finding - with an
# escape that is always available and is always a commit here.
#
# WHAT IS MEASURED IS THE AGE OF THE STREAK, NOT THE AGE OF THE MIRROR. The clock starts at the
# OLDEST run of the current streak - the moment the mirror started being red and stayed red - so
# a mirror that has been green for a year reports 0 and a mirror that went red yesterday reports
# 1. A cap on anything else would fire on repositories that are exactly right, which is the
# quickest way to teach somebody that a check is noise.
#
# THE CAP IS 14 DAYS, for the reasons tests/bin/ported-drift argues at length and which apply
# unchanged here: it must be under the 21 days this defect actually reached, and it must clear a
# normal working fortnight so that ordinary work is not punished. 14 is two clear weeks between
# a mirror going red and this repository being obliged to say something about it.
#
# THE ESCAPE, AND WHY IT KEEPS D-020 INTACT. A streak past the cap is a finding UNLESS this file
# carries a dated acknowledgement pinned to that streak's newest commit. Writing one is a commit
# in this repository, so no state of the mirror can hold this repository red: the remedy is
# always available and always here. That is the sense in which the mirror's conclusion still does
# not decide this gate - what decides it is whether this repository has ANSWERED a fortnight-old
# red, and silence is the only thing that fails.
#
# THE ACKNOWLEDGEMENT IS PINNED TO A SHA ON PURPOSE. A new push produces a new run; if that run
# is red too, the streak's newest sha changes and the acknowledgement stops applying. Answering
# one red must never silence the next one.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THIS DOES NOT DO.
#
#   * It does not change tests/bin/watch-gate. That script's mirror section stays exactly as it
#     is, including its own exit-status guarantee; this is the half that runs unasked, and the
#     two answer the same question from opposite ends.
#   * It does not read a job log, only the runs API. Which job inside the workflow failed is a
#     question for the person who opens the run, and reading logs would need a token.
#   * It does not add a CI job. It runs inside `agora-invariants`, through gate-a-wave1.sh.
#
# Contract (shared by every check in tests/bin/):
#   scope:    the slug, the branch and the declared workflow list
#   examined: how many runs the API returned, and over what page size
#   read:     how many were usable, and how many were not
#   findings: M, each printed as  subject:field  reason
#   exit 0 iff M == 0 and the API answered
#   exit 1 if M > 0                     (provenance, or an unanswered streak past the cap)
#   exit 2 if the API could not be read (the third state; the gate tolerates it)
#
# House rules for tests/bin/ (T-321(c)): `wc -l` never `grep -c` for a compared value; numeric
# guards defaulted ONLY where zero means FAIL; grep rc >= 2 is an error, never "no match".
#
# Usage: tests/bin/mirror-streak [--slug <owner/repo>] [--branch <name>]
#                                [--max-red-days <n>] [--page <n>] [--api-host <url>]
#        (run from anywhere; it cd's to the repo root)
#
# The five options exist so that every branch below can be falsified, and they were all used
# before this file was committed: --api-host against a local fake API is how the red-streak and
# the cap branches were watched firing, because the real mirror is green and cannot be made to
# demonstrate them. The gate passes none of the five: gate-a-wave1.sh asserts the cap line reads
# `14 days (default)`, so the number cannot be loosened from the call site without moving a check
# a human has to look at.

set -u
# No `set -e`: a finding must be recorded and counted, not abort the run.

SCRIPT_DIR=$(CDPATH= cd -- "$(dirname -- "$0")" && pwd)
REPO_ROOT=$(CDPATH= cd -- "$SCRIPT_DIR/../.." && pwd)
cd "$REPO_ROOT" || { echo "FATAL: cannot cd to repo root $REPO_ROOT"; exit 1; }

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- declarations --
# THE SLUG IS DECLARED, NOT DERIVED FROM A GIT REMOTE, and that is a requirement rather than a
# style choice. A drupalci runner clones from drupalcode and has no remote named `github` at all,
# so a script that read one would degrade to "nothing to check" in the only environment this file
# exists to run in - and would report that silence as a clean run. The remote is used as a
# CROSS-CHECK where it exists, below, which is the opposite direction.
MIRROR_SLUG='andresmoreno28/agora_transparency'
# Set by --slug. The cross-check in step 2 compares this file's DECLARATION against the remote,
# so when an operator overrides the declaration on the command line there is nothing left to
# cross-check and the mismatch becomes a note rather than a finding - printed either way, because
# a guard that silently stops applying is worse than one that says it has.
SLUG_OVERRIDDEN=0
API_HOST='https://api.github.com'
BRANCH=''
MAX_RED_DAYS=14
MAX_RED_DEFAULT=14
PAGE=30
WORKFLOW_DIR='.github/workflows'

# The workflows this repository knows the mirror runs. Declared for the reason the header gives:
# an undeclared workflow whose conclusion nobody reads is the original defect, one file over.
DECLARED_WORKFLOWS='.github/workflows/phpunit.yml'

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the acknowledgement register --
# EMPTY IS THE CORRECT STATE and it is the state on the day this file was written: the mirror is
# green. An entry here is a statement that a streak past the cap has been looked at and is not
# being fixed yet, with the reason and the date, pinned to the newest commit of that streak.
#
# Leave all three empty to arm the cap. Fill all three to answer one specific streak.
ACK_HEAD_SHA=''
ACK_ON=''
ACK_WHY=''

while [ "$#" -gt 0 ]; do
  case "$1" in
    --slug) shift; [ "$#" -gt 0 ] || { echo "FATAL: --slug needs a value"; exit 1; }; MIRROR_SLUG=$1; SLUG_OVERRIDDEN=1 ;;
    --branch) shift; [ "$#" -gt 0 ] || { echo "FATAL: --branch needs a value"; exit 1; }; BRANCH=$1 ;;
    --api-host) shift; [ "$#" -gt 0 ] || { echo "FATAL: --api-host needs a value"; exit 1; }; API_HOST=$1 ;;
    --max-red-days)
      shift
      [ "$#" -gt 0 ] || { echo "FATAL: --max-red-days needs a number"; exit 1; }
      case "$1" in
        ''|*[!0-9]*) echo "FATAL: --max-red-days wants a non-negative integer, got [$1]"; exit 1 ;;
      esac
      MAX_RED_DAYS=$1 ;;
    --page)
      shift
      [ "$#" -gt 0 ] || { echo "FATAL: --page needs a number"; exit 1; }
      case "$1" in
        ''|*[!0-9]*) echo "FATAL: --page wants a positive integer, got [$1]"; exit 1 ;;
      esac
      [ "$1" -gt 0 ] || { echo "FATAL: --page 0 would examine nothing"; exit 1; }
      PAGE=$1 ;;
    -h|--help)
      sed -n '/^# Usage:/,/^$/p' "$0" | sed 's/^# \{0,1\}//'
      exit 0 ;;
    *)
      # Refused rather than ignored: a check that silently accepts a misspelled flag runs its
      # DEFAULT and prints a clean result, which reads exactly like the thing that was asked for.
      echo "FATAL: unknown option [$1]. Run with --help."
      exit 1 ;;
  esac
  shift
done

C_OK=""; C_BAD=""; C_OFF=""; C_DIM=""
if [ -t 1 ]; then
  C_OK=$'\033[32m'; C_BAD=$'\033[31m'; C_OFF=$'\033[0m'; C_DIM=$'\033[2m'
fi

FINDINGS=0
finding() { # <subject> <field> <reason>
  FINDINGS=$((FINDINGS + 1))
  printf '  %s%s:%s%s  %s\n' "$C_BAD" "$1" "$2" "$C_OFF" "$3"
}
note() { printf '  %s%s%s\n' "$C_DIM" "$1" "$C_OFF"; }

fatal() { # <reason> - no result at all, which is not a clean result (I-029).
  printf '\n%sFATAL:%s %s\n' "$C_BAD" "$C_OFF" "$1"
  printf 'This run has NO result, which is not a clean result (I-029).\n'
  exit 1
}

grep_fatal() { # <rc> <where>
  fatal "grep exited $1 while reading $2. A grep exit code of 2 or more is an error, never 'no match', and treating it as one would turn a broken read into a clean run."
}

not_read_banner() { # <reason...>
  printf '\n  %sNOT READ%s - %s\n' "$C_BAD" "$C_OFF" "$1"
  shift
  while [ "$#" -gt 0 ]; do printf '             %s\n' "$1"; shift; done
  printf '             %sThat is not "the mirror is fine"; it is "nothing here could see\n' "$C_BAD"
  printf '             the mirror". An absence of information reading as good news for three\n'
  printf '             weeks is the entire defect this file closes.%s\n' "$C_OFF"
}

if [ -z "$BRANCH" ]; then
  BRANCH=$(git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD 2>/dev/null || echo '')
  [ -n "$BRANCH" ] && [ "$BRANCH" != 'HEAD' ] || BRANCH='1.x'
fi

printf '=========================================================================================================\n'
printf 'mirror-streak - Agora - the GitHub mirror of this package, read anonymously (T-0623)\n'
printf 'repo: %s\n' "$REPO_ROOT"
printf 'date: %s\n' "$(date -u '+%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ')"
printf '=========================================================================================================\n'

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the tooling --
# EXERCISED, NOT LOCATED (I-026). `command -v` has been satisfied on this project's hosts by a
# stub that then failed at first real use.
printf '\ntooling\n'
HAVE_CURL=0
if command -v curl >/dev/null 2>&1 && curl --version >/dev/null 2>&1; then HAVE_CURL=1; fi
HAVE_PY=0
if [ "$(python3 -c 'print(1)' 2>/dev/null)" = '1' ]; then HAVE_PY=1; fi
note "curl:    $(if [ "$HAVE_CURL" -eq 1 ]; then curl --version 2>/dev/null | head -1; else printf 'ABSENT'; fi)"
note "python3: $(if [ "$HAVE_PY" -eq 1 ]; then python3 --version 2>/dev/null; else printf 'ABSENT'; fi)"

# ----------------------------------------------------- 1. the declared workflow list, offline --
# This half needs no network at all, and it runs before anything else so that a repository whose
# own declaration is wrong is told so even when the API is unreachable.
printf '\n1. the declared workflow list against %s/ - offline, and always run\n' "$WORKFLOW_DIR"

DECLARED_N=0
while IFS= read -r w; do
  [ -n "$w" ] || continue
  DECLARED_N=$((DECLARED_N + 1))
  if [ ! -r "$w" ]; then
    finding 'workflows' 'declared' "[$w] is declared here but is not a readable file in this repository. A declaration that names nothing cannot be compared against anything, and the comparison below would silently shrink."
  fi
done <<EOF
$DECLARED_WORKFLOWS
EOF

# T-321(b): defaulted because zero means FAIL here - the safe direction of I-031. An empty
# declaration would make every comparison below pass by construction (I-028).
if [ "${DECLARED_N:-0}" -eq 0 ]; then
  fatal 'the declared workflow list is empty. An empty list agrees with any mirror, and reports that agreement as a clean run.'
fi

ON_DISK=''
ON_DISK_N=0
if [ -d "$WORKFLOW_DIR" ]; then
  ON_DISK=$(find "$WORKFLOW_DIR" -maxdepth 1 -type f \( -name '*.yml' -o -name '*.yaml' \) 2>/dev/null | sed 's#^\./##' | sort)
  ON_DISK_N=$(printf '%s\n' "$ON_DISK" | grep -v '^$' | wc -l | tr -d '[:space:]')
fi
note "declared: $DECLARED_N - on disk: $ON_DISK_N"

while IFS= read -r f; do
  [ -n "$f" ] || continue
  _found=no
  while IFS= read -r d; do
    [ -n "$d" ] || continue
    [ "$f" = "$d" ] && _found=yes
  done <<EOF
$DECLARED_WORKFLOWS
EOF
  if [ "$_found" = no ]; then
    finding 'workflows' 'undeclared' "$f exists in this repository and is not in DECLARED_WORKFLOWS. A workflow whose conclusion nobody reads is the defect this file exists to close, and the second one arrives without ceremony. Declare it here in the same commit that adds it."
  fi
done <<EOF
$ON_DISK
EOF

# ----------------------------------------------------- 2. the local remote, where there is one --
# A CROSS-CHECK AND NOT A SOURCE. In CI there is no `github` remote and this prints a note; on a
# maintainer's checkout there is one, and a slug that disagrees with it means this file is
# watching a different repository from the one this tree pushes to.
printf '\n2. the declared slug against the local `github` remote, where one exists\n'
LOCAL_URL=$(git config --get remote.github.url 2>/dev/null || true)
if [ -z "$LOCAL_URL" ]; then
  note "no remote named \`github\` in this checkout - which is the normal state on a CI runner, where the clone comes from drupalcode. The declared slug [$MIRROR_SLUG] is NOT corroborated here."
else
  _s="$LOCAL_URL"
  _s="${_s#https://github.com/}"; _s="${_s#http://github.com/}"
  _s="${_s#git@github.com:}";     _s="${_s#ssh://git@github.com/}"
  _s="${_s%.git}"
  if [ "$_s" = "$MIRROR_SLUG" ]; then
    note "remote.github.url parses to [$_s], which is the declared slug"
  elif [ "$SLUG_OVERRIDDEN" -eq 1 ]; then
    note "remote.github.url parses to [$_s] and --slug asked for [$MIRROR_SLUG]. NOT a finding: the declaration was overridden from the command line, so there is no declaration left to cross-check. The gate never passes --slug."
  else
    finding 'slug' 'remote' "this checkout pushes its mirror to [$_s] and this file declares [$MIRROR_SLUG]. One of the two is watching a repository nobody is pushing to, and a green from the wrong repository is worse than no green at all."
  fi
fi

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the fetcher --
# api_get <url> <outfile> -> sets HTTP and TRANSPORT.
#   TRANSPORT != 0  the request never got an answer      -> NOT READ
#   HTTP == 200     an answer                            -> usable
#   HTTP == 404     an answer, and a negative one        -> a FINDING at the caller
#   403 / 429 / 5xx the server declining to answer       -> NOT READ (retried once)
# GitHub answers 403 with X-RateLimit-Remaining: 0 when an anonymous caller is over its 60 an
# hour. That is the server saying nothing about the question, not a statement about the mirror,
# so it is the third state and never a finding.
HTTP=0
TRANSPORT=0
api_get() { # <url> <outfile>
  _u=$1; _o=$2
  _attempt=0
  while : ; do
    _attempt=$((_attempt + 1))
    HTTP=$(curl -sS --connect-timeout 15 --max-time 60 \
             -H 'Accept: application/vnd.github+json' \
             -H 'X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2022-11-28' \
             -o "$_o" -w '%{http_code}' "$_u" 2>/dev/null)
    TRANSPORT=$?
    [ -n "$HTTP" ] || HTTP=0
    if [ "$TRANSPORT" -eq 0 ]; then
      case "$HTTP" in
        403|429|5??)
          if [ "$_attempt" -lt 2 ]; then sleep 5; continue; fi ;;
      esac
    fi
    break
  done
}

WORK_DIR=$(mktemp -d -t mirror-streak.XXXXXX) || fatal 'mktemp -d failed - there is nowhere to put the API answers.'
trap 'rm -rf "$WORK_DIR"' EXIT INT TERM

EXAMINED=0
READ_N=0
UNREAD_N=0
COMPLETED=0
STREAK=0
STREAK_OLDEST_AGE=0
NET_STATE='NOT READ'
UNREACHABLE=''

if [ "$HAVE_CURL" -eq 0 ]; then
  UNREACHABLE='curl is not installed, so no request can be made at all.'
elif [ "$HAVE_PY" -eq 0 ]; then
  UNREACHABLE='python3 is not installed, so the API answers cannot be parsed.'
fi

API="$API_HOST/repos/$MIRROR_SLUG"

# --------------------------------------------------- 3. the preflight, which proves four things --
if [ -z "$UNREACHABLE" ]; then
  printf '\n3. reaching %s\n' "$MIRROR_SLUG"
  META="$WORK_DIR/meta.json"
  api_get "$API" "$META"
  if [ "$TRANSPORT" -ne 0 ]; then
    UNREACHABLE="curl exited $TRANSPORT reaching $API_HOST - the request got no answer at all (DNS, connectivity, proxy or TLS)."
  elif [ "$HTTP" = '404' ]; then
    finding 'slug' 'declared' "$API_HOST answered 404 for [$MIRROR_SLUG]. That is the API stating a fact - no such public repository - and it is a finding rather than an outage, because a commit here can correct the declaration."
    UNREACHABLE="the declared repository does not exist, so there are no runs to examine."
  elif [ "$HTTP" != '200' ]; then
    UNREACHABLE="$API_HOST answered HTTP $HTTP for the repository itself. 403 with no rate left and 5xx are the server declining to answer; neither is a statement about the mirror."
  else
    FULL=$(python3 -c 'import json,sys;print((json.load(open(sys.argv[1],encoding="utf-8")) or {}).get("full_name") or "")' "$META" 2>/dev/null)
    if [ -z "$FULL" ]; then
      UNREACHABLE='the repository endpoint answered 200 with something this could not parse as JSON carrying a full_name.'
    elif [ "$FULL" != "$MIRROR_SLUG" ]; then
      finding 'slug' 'full_name' "the API calls it [$FULL] and this file declares [$MIRROR_SLUG]. A renamed repository still answers on its old path by redirect, so this is the one request that notices."
    else
      note "full_name: $FULL - the declared slug, confirmed by the API"
    fi
  fi
fi

# ------------------------------------------------- 4. the workflows the mirror has actually run --
if [ -z "$UNREACHABLE" ]; then
  printf '\n4. the workflows the mirror declares, against the list above\n'
  WFJ="$WORK_DIR/workflows.json"
  api_get "$API/actions/workflows?per_page=100" "$WFJ"
  if [ "$TRANSPORT" -ne 0 ] || [ "$HTTP" != '200' ]; then
    note "the workflows endpoint gave no usable answer (curl $TRANSPORT, HTTP $HTTP) - the run walk below still ran, and it names undeclared workflows too"
  else
    REMOTE_WF=$(python3 -c 'import json,sys
d = json.load(open(sys.argv[1], encoding="utf-8")) or {}
for w in d.get("workflows") or []:
    p = w.get("path") or ""
    if p:
        print(p)' "$WFJ" 2>/dev/null | sort -u)
    REMOTE_WF_N=$(printf '%s\n' "$REMOTE_WF" | grep -v '^$' | wc -l | tr -d '[:space:]')
    note "the mirror declares $REMOTE_WF_N workflow(s)"
    while IFS= read -r r; do
      [ -n "$r" ] || continue
      _ok=no
      while IFS= read -r d; do
        [ -n "$d" ] || continue
        [ "$r" = "$d" ] && _ok=yes
      done <<EOF
$DECLARED_WORKFLOWS
EOF
      [ "$_ok" = yes ] || finding 'workflows' 'remote' "the mirror runs [$r], which is not in DECLARED_WORKFLOWS. Its conclusion is being read by nobody here."
    done <<EOF
$REMOTE_WF
EOF
  fi
fi

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ 5. the streak --
STREAK_LINES=''
if [ -z "$UNREACHABLE" ]; then
  printf '\n5. the runs on branch %s\n' "$BRANCH"
  RUNS="$WORK_DIR/runs.json"
  api_get "$API/actions/runs?branch=$BRANCH&per_page=$PAGE" "$RUNS"
  if [ "$TRANSPORT" -ne 0 ] || [ "$HTTP" != '200' ]; then
    UNREACHABLE="the runs endpoint gave no usable answer (curl $TRANSPORT, HTTP $HTTP)."
  else
    STREAK_LINES=$(MS_DECLARED="$DECLARED_WORKFLOWS" python3 -c '
import json, os, sys, datetime
# cspell:ignore fromisoformat

# The whole streak computation in one place, because doing it in shell would mean parsing ISO
# timestamps with `date -d`, which is not portable to every runner this has to work on.
d = json.load(open(sys.argv[1], encoding="utf-8")) or {}
runs = d.get("workflow_runs") or []
print("EXAMINED %d" % len(runs))
declared = {w.strip() for w in os.environ["MS_DECLARED"].splitlines() if w.strip()}

seen_paths = set()
completed = []
for r in runs:
    p = r.get("path") or ""
    if p:
        seen_paths.add(p)
    if r.get("status") == "completed":
        completed.append(r)

for p in sorted(seen_paths - declared):
    print("UNDECLARED %s" % p)

print("COMPLETED %d" % len(completed))
if not completed:
    print("NO_STREAK none of the runs examined has completed, so no conclusion can be counted")
    raise SystemExit

now = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc)


def when(run):
    raw = run.get("updated_at") or run.get("created_at") or ""
    try:
        return datetime.datetime.fromisoformat(raw.replace("Z", "+00:00"))
    except ValueError:
        return None


streak = 0
for r in completed:
    if r.get("conclusion") == "success":
        break
    streak += 1

print("STREAK %d" % streak)
if streak:
    conclusion_set = sorted({(r.get("conclusion") or "unknown") for r in completed[:streak]})
    print("CONCLUSIONS %s" % ",".join(conclusion_set))
    print("NEWEST %s" % (completed[0].get("head_sha") or ""))
    oldest = when(completed[streak - 1])
    if oldest is None:
        print("AGE -1")
    else:
        print("AGE %d" % ((now - oldest).days))
        print("SINCE %s" % completed[streak - 1].get("updated_at"))
    for r in completed[:streak][:5]:
        print("RUN %s %s %s %s" % ((r.get("head_sha") or "")[:8],
                                   r.get("conclusion") or "unknown",
                                   r.get("updated_at") or "?",
                                   r.get("html_url") or ""))
if streak < len(completed):
    ok = completed[streak]
    w = when(ok)
    print("LAST_OK %s %s %s" % ((ok.get("head_sha") or "")[:8],
                               ok.get("updated_at") or "?",
                               (now - w).days if w else -1))
else:
    print("NOOK no success in the %d completed run(s) examined - the streak below is a FLOOR, not a count" % len(completed))
' "$RUNS" 2>/dev/null)
    if [ -z "$STREAK_LINES" ]; then
      UNREACHABLE='the runs endpoint answered 200 with something the parser could not read as a run list.'
    fi
  fi
fi

if [ -n "$UNREACHABLE" ]; then
  not_read_banner "$UNREACHABLE"
else
  NET_STATE='READ'
  EXAMINED=$(printf '%s\n' "$STREAK_LINES" | sed -n 's/^EXAMINED //p' | head -1)
  COMPLETED=$(printf '%s\n' "$STREAK_LINES" | sed -n 's/^COMPLETED //p' | head -1)
  STREAK=$(printf '%s\n' "$STREAK_LINES" | sed -n 's/^STREAK //p' | head -1)
  [ -n "$EXAMINED" ] || EXAMINED=0
  [ -n "$COMPLETED" ] || COMPLETED=0
  [ -n "$STREAK" ] || STREAK=0
  READ_N=$COMPLETED
  UNREAD_N=$((EXAMINED - COMPLETED))

  while IFS= read -r u; do
    [ -n "$u" ] || continue
    finding 'workflows' 'ran' "the mirror has RUN [$u] on this branch and it is not in DECLARED_WORKFLOWS."
  done <<EOF
$(printf '%s\n' "$STREAK_LINES" | sed -n 's/^UNDECLARED //p')
EOF

  if [ "${EXAMINED:-0}" -eq 0 ]; then
    not_read_banner "the API answered with NO RUNS AT ALL on branch $BRANCH." \
      'That is an unread mirror, not a green one. Has this branch ever been pushed to `github`?'
    NET_STATE='NOT READ'
    UNREACHABLE='no runs'
  else
    note "$EXAMINED run(s) returned (page size $PAGE), $COMPLETED of them completed"
    _no_streak=$(printf '%s\n' "$STREAK_LINES" | sed -n 's/^NO_STREAK //p' | head -1)
    if [ -n "$_no_streak" ]; then
      note "streak NOT COMPUTED - $_no_streak"
    elif [ "${STREAK:-0}" -eq 0 ]; then
      _last_ok=$(printf '%s\n' "$STREAK_LINES" | sed -n 's/^LAST_OK //p' | head -1)
      printf '  %s' "$C_OK"
      printf 'streak: 0 - the newest completed run on %s succeeded (%s)%s\n' \
        "$BRANCH" "$_last_ok" "$C_OFF"
    else
      _conclusions=$(printf '%s\n' "$STREAK_LINES" | sed -n 's/^CONCLUSIONS //p' | head -1)
      _age=$(printf '%s\n' "$STREAK_LINES" | sed -n 's/^AGE //p' | head -1)
      _since=$(printf '%s\n' "$STREAK_LINES" | sed -n 's/^SINCE //p' | head -1)
      _newest=$(printf '%s\n' "$STREAK_LINES" | sed -n 's/^NEWEST //p' | head -1)
      _nook=$(printf '%s\n' "$STREAK_LINES" | sed -n 's/^NOOK //p' | head -1)
      [ -n "$_age" ] || _age=-1
      STREAK_OLDEST_AGE=$_age
      if [ -n "$_nook" ]; then
        printf '  %sRED STREAK: >= %s consecutive non-success completed run(s) - %s%s\n' \
          "$C_BAD" "$STREAK" "$_nook" "$C_OFF"
      else
        printf '  %sRED STREAK: %s consecutive non-success completed run(s) on %s%s\n' \
          "$C_BAD" "$STREAK" "$BRANCH" "$C_OFF"
      fi
      printf '  %s' "$C_BAD"
      printf 'conclusions: %s - oldest of the streak: %s (%s day(s) ago)%s\n' \
        "$_conclusions" "${_since:-unknown}" "$_age" "$C_OFF"
      printf '%s\n' "$STREAK_LINES" | sed -n 's/^RUN /    /p'
      _last_ok=$(printf '%s\n' "$STREAK_LINES" | sed -n 's/^LAST_OK //p' | head -1)
      if [ -n "$_last_ok" ]; then
        printf '  %s' "$C_DIM"
        printf 'last success: %s%s\n' "$_last_ok" "$C_OFF"
      fi

      # THE CAP. A streak is data; a streak nobody has answered for a fortnight is a finding.
      if [ "$_age" -lt 0 ] 2>/dev/null; then
        finding 'streak' 'age' "the mirror has been red for $STREAK consecutive run(s) and the oldest of them carries a timestamp this host could not parse. An age that cannot be measured has not been shown to be inside the $MAX_RED_DAYS-day cap, and 'unknown' is not 'recent'."
      elif [ "$_age" -gt "$MAX_RED_DAYS" ]; then
        if [ -n "$ACK_HEAD_SHA" ] && [ "$ACK_HEAD_SHA" = "$_newest" ]; then
          note "past the cap, and ANSWERED: acknowledged $ACK_ON for [${_newest}] - $ACK_WHY"
        else
          finding 'streak' 'cap' "the mirror has been red for $STREAK consecutive run(s) across $_age days, past the $MAX_RED_DAYS-day cap. Being red is not itself a finding here and never turns this gate red on its own; being red for this long with nothing in this repository saying anything about it is. Answer it in ONE of two ways, both of them commits HERE: fix the workflow under $WORKFLOW_DIR/, or fill ACK_HEAD_SHA (=$_newest), ACK_ON and ACK_WHY in $0 with the reason it stays red. The acknowledgement is pinned to that sha, so the next red push re-arms this."
        fi
      fi
    fi
  fi
fi

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- summary --
printf '\n=========================================================================================================\n'
printf 'scope:    %s branch %s, %s workflow(s) declared\n' "$MIRROR_SLUG" "$BRANCH" "$DECLARED_N"
printf 'cap:      %s\n' "$(if [ "$MAX_RED_DAYS" -eq "$MAX_RED_DEFAULT" ]; then printf '%s days (default)' "$MAX_RED_DAYS"; else printf '%s days (OVERRIDDEN with --max-red-days; the gate never passes it)' "$MAX_RED_DAYS"; fi)"
printf 'examined: %s run(s) returned by the API (page size %s)\n' "$EXAMINED" "$PAGE"
printf 'read:     %s completed, %s still running or queued\n' "$READ_N" "$UNREAD_N"
printf 'streak:   %s consecutive non-success completed run(s); oldest %s day(s)\n' \
  "$STREAK" "$STREAK_OLDEST_AGE"
printf 'findings: %s  (a streak inside the cap is never one - only broken provenance, and a streak left unanswered too long)\n' "$FINDINGS"
printf 'network:  %s - %s\n' "$NET_STATE" \
  "$(if [ "$NET_STATE" = 'READ' ]; then printf '%s answered anonymously; no token was used or needed' "$API_HOST"; else printf '%s said nothing this run could use, so the streak above is not a statement about the mirror' "$API_HOST"; fi)"
printf '=========================================================================================================\n'

if [ "$FINDINGS" -ne 0 ]; then
  printf '%s%s%s\n' "$C_BAD" "mirror-streak: $FINDINGS finding(s) - each one fixable by a commit in THIS repository" "$C_OFF"
  exit 1
fi
if [ "$NET_STATE" != 'READ' ]; then
  printf '%s%s%s\n' "$C_BAD" "mirror-streak: the mirror was NOT READ - this run has no answer about it, which is not a clean answer about it" "$C_OFF"
  exit 2
fi
if [ "${STREAK:-0}" -ne 0 ]; then
  CAP_WORDS="inside the $MAX_RED_DAYS-day cap"
  if [ "$STREAK_OLDEST_AGE" -gt "$MAX_RED_DAYS" ] 2>/dev/null; then
    CAP_WORDS="past the $MAX_RED_DAYS-day cap and ANSWERED by the acknowledgement above"
  fi
  printf '%s%s%s\n' "$C_DIM" "mirror-streak: the mirror is RED - $STREAK consecutive non-success run(s), $STREAK_OLDEST_AGE day(s) old, $CAP_WORDS. D-020 keeps the mirror informative, so this does not fail the gate; it is printed on every push so that nobody has to notice an email." "$C_OFF"
  exit 0
fi
printf '%s%s%s\n' "$C_OK" 'mirror-streak: every declared workflow accounted for, and the newest completed run on this branch succeeded' "$C_OFF"
exit 0
